Assumption challenge
--------------------
This session does not use runners or points as tournament vertices.
It uses proof obligations: clean C-shells, odd-prime shortcut rows,
Moser slab count, Eisenstein symmetry, and exact-upper side channels.
The quotient preserves which theorem route becomes simpler and destroys
the raw continuous LRC orbit and the concrete planar embedding.
